title: Cisco Nexus: Spanning-Tree Topology Changes per VLAN
agents: snmp
catalog: hw/network/cisco
license: GPLv2
distribution: nxos_stp_tcn
description:
 Monitors spanning-tree topology changes of each VLAN on Cisco Nexus (NX-OS)
 switches. Data is collected by the special agent "Cisco Nexus STP topology
 changes (SNMPv3 VLAN contexts)", which reads the VLAN list from
 CISCO-CONTEXT-MAPPING-MIB and queries the BRIDGE-MIB objects
 dot1dStpTopChanges and dot1dStpTimeSinceTopologyChange in each VLAN's numeric
 SNMPv3 context.

 The service is {CRIT} if the most recent topology change happened within the
 configured critical window (default: 12 hours) and optionally {WARN} within a
 longer warning window. Otherwise it is {OK}. A VLAN that never had a topology
 change is always {OK}, because the NX-OS timer then counts from the start of
 spanning tree (e.g. a reboot) rather than from a change.

 Optionally, upper levels can be set on the topology change rate (changes per
 hour). A decreasing counter (reboot, Counter32 wrap) yields no rate for that
 check interval.

 If the SNMP context of a VLAN does not answer, only that service becomes
 {UNKNOWN}.

 Verified on Nexus 9000 C93240YC-FX2 with NX-OS 10.2(5). NX-OS 10.4(5) on
 C93180YC-FX3 does not provide these BRIDGE-MIB objects via SNMP.

item:
 The VLAN ID.

discovery:
 One service is created for each VLAN that has spanning-tree data. The ruleset
 "Cisco Nexus STP topology VLAN discovery" can restrict discovery to, or exclude,
 specific VLANs.
